    <!-- ================= How to use / FAQ ================= -->
    <string name="faq_title">How to use &amp; FAQ</string>
    <string name="howto_step_1">Open WhatsApp and view the Updates tab so statuses are downloaded to your phone.</string>
    <string name="howto_step_2">Open Status Saver. Your statuses appear under Images and Videos.</string>
    <string name="howto_step_3">Tap the download button to save a status to your gallery.</string>
    <string name="howto_step_4">Find your downloads in the Saved tab or in your Gallery (Pictures/StatusSaver and Movies/StatusSaver).</string>
    <string name="faq_q1">Why don’t I see any statuses?</string>
    <string name="faq_a1">WhatsApp only stores statuses after they load in its Updates tab. Open the Updates tab once, return here and pull down to refresh.</string>
    <string name="faq_q2">Will the person know I saved their status?</string>
    <string name="faq_a2">This app only reads files that are already on your device. It never contacts WhatsApp servers and sends nothing to anyone.</string>
    <string name="faq_q3">Why does the app need folder access?</string>
    <string name="faq_a3">Android protects the status folder. You approve access to that single folder once; no other files are read.</string>
    <string name="faq_q4">Where are saved files stored?</string>
    <string name="faq_a4">Images go to Pictures/StatusSaver and videos to Movies/StatusSaver. They appear in your gallery immediately.</string>
    <string name="faq_q5">Statuses disappeared after 24 hours?</string>
    <string name="faq_a5">WhatsApp deletes statuses after 24 hours. Save the ones you want to keep, or turn on Auto-save in Settings.</string>
    <string name="faq_q6">Does it work with WhatsApp Business?</string>
    <string name="faq_a6">Yes. Use the app switcher at the top of the home screen and grant access to the WhatsApp Business folder.</string>

